{"name":"Tried & True Blue","hex":"#494f62","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tried","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tested, hence, proven to be firm or reliable.","Put on trial, taken before a lawcourt."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of try"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tried"},{"term":"true","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Conforming to the actual state of reality or fact; factually correct.","As an ellipsis of \"(while) it is true (that)\", used to start a sentence"]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Accurately; in alignment.","Truthfully."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trial","blocks":[{"text":"In law, a trial is a coming together of parties to a dispute, to present information in a tribunal, a formal setting with the authority to adjudicate claims or disputes. One form of tribunal is a court. The tribunal, which may occur before a judge, jury, or other designated trier of fact, aims to achieve a resolution to their dispute."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Le_Lit_de_justice_de_Vend%C3%B4me.jpg/330px-Le_Lit_de_justice_de_Vend%C3%B4me.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trial"},{"title":"Ampersand","blocks":[{"text":"The ampersand, also known as the and sign, is the logogram &, representing the conjunction \"and\". It originated as a ligature of the word et."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Et_sign.svg/330px-Et_sign.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampersand"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg/500px-Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg/500px-Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Old Bailey in London, 1808","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOld_Bailey_Microcosm_edited.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/The_Trial_of_the_66_in_Le_Monde_illustr%C3%A9_of_27_January_1883_%281%29.jpg/500px-The_Trial_of_the_66_in_Le_Monde_illustr%C3%A9_of_27_January_1883_%281%29.jpg?utm_sou